<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>{{ site_title }}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>{{ site_heading }}</h1>
    <p>{{ site_subheading }}</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="card">
      <h2>What this page proves</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Ansible installed Apache automatically — no manual apt install</li>
        <li>Ansible created the users listed in the inventory variables</li>
        <li>The firewall allows only SSH, HTTP and HTTPS</li>
        <li>The application files were deployed by Ansible, and Apache was restarted only because a file changed</li>
        <li>Re-running the playbook changes nothing (idempotency)</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Server facts (rendered by Ansible)</h2>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Hostname</th><td>{{ ansible_facts['hostname'] }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Operating system</th><td>{{ ansible_facts['distribution'] }} {{ ansible_facts['distribution_version'] }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>IP address</th><td>{{ ansible_facts['default_ipv4']['address'] }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Web server</th><td>Apache2 on port {{ apache_port }}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Deployed at</th><td>{{ ansible_facts['date_time']['iso8601'] }}</td></tr>
      </table>
      <p><button id="demoBtn">Click me — JavaScript works too</button></p>
      <p id="demoMsg"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>How it was deployed</h2>
      <pre>ansible-playbook playbooks/site.yml</pre>
      <p>Roles: <code>common</code> &rarr; <code>users</code> &rarr; <code>firewall</code> &rarr; <code>apache</code> &rarr; <code>app</code></p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>Deployed with Ansible &bull; Apache &bull; Project 10 — DevOps-Projects-2026 &bull; Naim Khan</p>
  </footer>

  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
